      "id": "df898a95-9704-409f-b131-c82d7d3a5f55",
      "type": "FREE_RESPONSE",
      "data": {
        "body": "(a) List ALL assumptions which should be satisfied to conduct inference in a simple linear regression analysis.",
        "solution": "Assumptions:\n1) SRS: The response (server traffic) is obtained as a simple random sample for each\nfixed \ud835\udc99 (investment). It is okay if they mention that the pairs are SRS.\n2) Linearity: Assume that the relationship between server traffic and investment dollars\nis linear.\n3) Homogeneity/Constant Variance: Assume that the residual errors have common\nvariance.\n4) Normality: Assume that the residual errors are normally distribued.",
        "answerChoices": []
      },
